    "S1": "A U part that holds \"worse (U)\" reads \"worse (U)\" also when an equivalence grade prints beside it (LN-36: both print) or the note \"significant, below the smallest effect of interest\" does: it is eligible. Alternative: \"worse (U)\" with an equivalence grade is an equivalent contrast (the HarmBench claim reader's R3), not eligible.",
